    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen `ui2` is enabled, opening an already-open file in another Neovim instance results in the error `E812: Autocommands changed buffer or buffer name`.\n\nTo be precise the error is related to the warning message that appears when opened second time: `W325: Ignoring swapfile from Nvim process`.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/46eda795-707b-42d6-87a4-936cd2c6d5f2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nYes, open **two** instances with the same file:\n\n```\necho 'Neovim is great' > test.txt\nnvim --noplugin -u repro.lua test.txt\nnvim --noplugin -u repro.lua test.txt\n```\n\n```lua\n-- repro.lua\n-- vim.opt.shortmess:append(\"A\") -- Toggle me\nrequire(\"vim._core.ui2\").enable()\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo error\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1391+g 1deeff9c38\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Btw\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty 0.17.0 (94e7c887)\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nalacritty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
